   "source": "community",
   "text": "Now that I've seen this land and have heard the sound of the earth here, I think I am glad I made the journey. \r\n\r\nAh, forgive me. I am thinking aloud. I am called Stonetorch, and I come here seeking knowledge of a brilliant white stone that some say fell from the sky and came to rest in the hills over yonder. Some among my people believe that this is a tear wept from An'she, the eye of the Earth Mother herself.\r\n\r\nI don't know if I believe that, but I do intend to see this phenomenon for myself and make my own judgement.",
